Write $8=8e^{2k\pi i}$, so $z=2e^{2k\pi i/3}$, $k=0,1,2$:

- $k=0$: $z=2$;
- $k=1$: $z=2\left(\cos\tfrac{2\pi}3+i\sin\tfrac{2\pi}3\right)=2\left(-\tfrac12+i\tfrac{\sqrt3}2\right)=-1+i\sqrt3$;
- $k=2$: $z=-1-i\sqrt3$.

Alternatively $z^3-8=(z-2)(z^2+2z+4)$ and $z=\dfrac{-2\pm\sqrt{4-16}}{2}=-1\pm i\sqrt3$. Check: $|{-1+i\sqrt3}|=2$ and the three roots are equally spaced by $120^\circ$ on the circle of radius $2$. **Answer: D.**

$M\circ N$ means "apply $N$ first, then $M$": $(M\circ N)(x)=M(N(x))$. Reading the permutations as $M:1\mapsto2,\ 2\mapsto3,\ 3\mapsto1$ and $N:1\mapsto3,\ 2\mapsto2,\ 3\mapsto1$:

- $1\xrightarrow{N}3\xrightarrow{M}1$;
- $2\xrightarrow{N}2\xrightarrow{M}3$;
- $3\xrightarrow{N}1\xrightarrow{M}2$.

So $M\circ N=\begin{pmatrix}1&2&3\\1&3&2\end{pmatrix}$, a transposition of $2$ and $3$. (If the order of composition were reversed, $N\circ M$ would be $\begin{pmatrix}1&2&3\\2&1&3\end{pmatrix}$, which is option D: the order matters because $S_3$ is non-Abelian.) **Answer: B.**
